# fixes: F1
# A reclaim that finds a workspace an earlier one left `releasing` never
# publishes `active` once that earlier one got past its forget:
# finish_going_back keeps the row `releasing`, begin_reclaim accepts a
# `releasing` row the reclaim went back for (with no expiry check), and a
# failed forget of a jj workspace that is already gone leaves the
# workspace `releasing` for the next reclaim instead of rolling back.
<<<
    /\ \/ Fail /\ Exit(p) /\ UNCHANGED <<dbState, mem>>
       \/ dbState' = "active" /\ mem' = "active" /\ Goto(p, "check")
          /\ UNCHANGED <<lock, failLeft>>
===
    /\ Goto(p, "begin") /\ UNCHANGED <<dbState, mem, lock, failLeft>>
>>>
<<<
BeginOk(p) == dbState = "active" /\ (p = "release" \/ lease = "past")
===
BeginOk(p) == \/ dbState = "active" /\ (p = "release" \/ lease = "past")
              \/ dbState = "releasing" /\ wentBack[p]
>>>
<<<
       \/ RollBack(1) /\ Exit(p) /\ UNCHANGED <<jjws, handle>>
===
       \/ jjws /\ RollBack(1) /\ Exit(p) /\ UNCHANGED <<jjws, handle>>
       \/ ~jjws /\ Fail /\ Exit(p)
          /\ UNCHANGED <<jjws, handle, dbState, mem, tracked>>
>>>
